risks of colonization, to

00:37:03.330 --> 00:37:05.970
valorize, the colonists and to
make a case for the good

00:37:05.970 --> 00:37:09.600
consequences that will arise
from the colonial act, right,

00:37:09.600 --> 00:37:14.250
you will become a hero, you will
realize utopian visions that you

00:37:14.250 --> 00:37:19.050
have on Earth. So why, why these
differences? What my account for

00:37:19.050 --> 00:37:22.230
it. So in thinking about these
different cases, one thing that

00:37:22.230 --> 00:37:25.920
occurred to me is that in our
modern context, right, we have a

00:37:25.920 --> 00:37:30.000
real faith in sort of the techno
scientific capacity to address

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:33.600
risks in a way that early modern
folks did not. So they had to,

00:37:33.600 --> 00:37:37.320
in fact, offer reassurances Why?
Well, because they couldn't

00:37:37.320 --> 00:37:40.560
really say that they could solve
the problems. But now, we have

00:37:40.560 --> 00:37:42.720
this sort of belief in
technology and belief in the

00:37:42.720 --> 00:37:46.560
technological progress, such
that we can almost valorize

00:37:47.220 --> 00:37:52.680
these these moments of, of
colonialism as a way of showing

00:37:52.680 --> 00:37:56.100
our chops of a way of showing
how we can solve the problems

00:37:56.100 --> 00:37:59.790
and make ourselves heroes by
doing so. The other thing that's

